stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Uninitialized
    Uninitialized --> Initializing: Host calls ARA plugin initialization
    Initializing --> Ready: ARA DocumentController created and ready
    Ready --> PlugInAdded: Host adds plug-in to ARA document
    PlugInAdded --> PlugInRemoved: Host removes plug-in from document (or document closed)
    PlugInRemoved --> Ready: Plug-in removed but host still alive (can be re-added)
    Ready --> Uninitialized: Host uninitializes the ARA plug-in
    PlugInAdded --> OfflineRendering: Host initiates offline rendering (e.g., bounce, render-in-place)
    OfflineRendering --> PlugInAdded: Offline rendering completes
    PlugInAdded --> Analysis: Host requests analysis (e.g., chord detection, tempo analysis)
    Analysis --> PlugInAdded: Analysis completes
    %% Note: The ARA thread may call into the plug-in for DocumentController, PlaybackRenderer, EditorRenderer.
    %% We model the high-level lifecycle of the ARA plug-in instance within the host.